---
import Reference from '../../layouts/reference.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'set-up-the-workspace', text: 'Set up' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'run-the-documentation-site', text: 'Run the site' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'run-the-standalone-examples', text: 'Run the examples' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'build-shaders-and-api', text: 'Build shaders and API docs' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'check-your-changes', text: 'Check your changes' },
];
---
<Reference headings={headings} title="Development" description="Set up reparticle locally to make and test changes.">
  <h2 id={headings[0].slug}>{headings[0].text}</h2>
  <p>Install Node.js 24 or later and pnpm 10.32.1, then clone the repository:</p>
  <Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'git clone https://github.com/reparticlejs/reparticle.git\ncd reparticle\npnpm install'} lang="sh" />
  <h2 id={headings[1].slug}>{headings[1].text}</h2>
  <Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'pnpm dev:site'} lang="sh" />
  <p>Starts the website with the docs, lab, and examples. Open the URL shown in your terminal.</p>
  <h2 id={headings[2].slug}>{headings[2].text}</h2>
  <Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'pnpm dev'} lang="sh" />
  <p>Starts the example gallery on its own.
  </p>
  <p>Run these commands from the repository root. Both build the library packages before starting. After changing library code, stop and rerun the command to rebuild it. Restart <code>pnpm dev:site</code> after changing source comments or types to refresh the generated API docs.</p>
  <h2 id={headings[3].slug}>{headings[3].text}</h2>
  <p>Simulation is written in TypeScript with TypeGPU. Building core generates the WebGL2 shaders. Applications receive the generated shaders; they do not need TypeGPU or a build plugin.</p>
  <Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'pnpm --filter @reparticle/core build'} lang="sh" />
  <p>API pages come from the packages’ exported types and comments. Edit the source, then regenerate the pages:</p>
  <Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'pnpm --filter @reparticle/site build:api'} lang="sh" />
  <p>Do not edit generated shaders or API pages by hand. Both are rebuilt by <code>pnpm build</code>.</p>
  <p>See <a href={`${base}docs/development/architecture/`}>Particle architecture</a> for storage, updates, and resource ownership.</p>
  <h2 id={headings[4].slug}>{headings[4].text}</h2>
  <Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'pnpm check'} lang="sh" />
  <p>Tests include real WebGL2 simulation and Pixi rendering. <code>pnpm test</code> installs Chromium automatically when needed. CI installs Linux system dependencies separately.</p>
  <p>Checks formatting, lint, types, and tests, then builds the project. To fix formatting, run <code>pnpm format</code>.</p>
  <p><code>pnpm install</code> enables Git hooks. Commits check formatting and lint on staged files; pushes run type checks and tests.</p>
  <p>Type-aware linting first builds core and pixi so their exported types are available. Turbo reuses those builds when the packages have not changed.</p>
  <p>GitHub Actions runs <code>pnpm check</code> on pull requests and pushes to <code>main</code>. Publishing a package from this workspace also runs the full check first. Publishing a prebuilt tarball bypasses package hooks, so run <code>pnpm check</code> before packing a release.</p>
</Reference>
